WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.130
- We don't really play
games with our parents.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.130
- Oh, game playing, um...

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.640
- Probably, maybe once a month.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.340
- Video games, I usually am like, no.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.588
- I haven't really played
anything since the early 90's.

00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:13.982
- Once a week?

00:00:13.982 --> 00:00:15.350
- Mmm.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.685
- [Kid] No, Dad.
(soft playful music)

00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:18.900
No, no.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.345
- Family learning, let me think.

00:00:21.345 --> 00:00:23.730
(chuckling) Let me think.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.930
When her and some kids get together

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.490
to share experiences and
explore the world together.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.930
My name is Sinem Siyahhan.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.340
I'm an Associate Professor
of Educational Technology

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.793
and Learning Sciences
at Cal State San Marcos.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.923
My gaming skills are average.

00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:41.120
(mooing)

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.720
Sorry.
(laughs)

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.560
I just wanna make sure
that I can get some meat

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.080
out of this cow.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.190
My current work is inspired
by my experience as a child.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.990
Two parents are working long hours.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.320
They didn't have enough energy and time

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.200
to play with me and my brother,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.510
and we didn't really get
to spend time together.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.640
I try to play with my son

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.550
as much as I can.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.550
I value playing games.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:07.383
- Oh, there.

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:09.610
- Yes.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.930
So, for example, here,

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.998
we're exploring the farm.

00:01:13.998 --> 00:01:14.831
(pig squeals)

00:01:14.831 --> 00:01:17.060
And we're interacting with animals,

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.911
and my son is learning

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:19.930
(baby exclaims)

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.750
what sound each animal makes.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.146
What does the sheep say?

00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:25.339
(imitates bleating)

00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:26.660
(chuckling) Mah, yes.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.280
Engaging in play is important,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.200
whether it is digital

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.820
or non-digital play.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.420
We invite parents and
kids to play together.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.180
We're fortunate to have Alienware

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.320
provide gaming laptops for our families.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.830
- What I find really
interesting with Play2Connect,

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.070
it helps families grow these
shared values together.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:48.920
Hey, Sinem, how's it goin'?

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.520
- It's going well, how are you?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.560
- I'm doin' well, did everything show up?

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.200
- Yes, we have the laptops,
they're ready to go.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.834
I believe I am making positive impact

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.007
through video games.

00:01:59.007 --> 00:02:02.580
One of the problems that I
see is video games are framed

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.040
as a context of conflict
between parents and kids.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.680
What I'm trying to do is

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.530
to show parents and kids that video games

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.870
could be a context for togetherness,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.390
collaboration, problem solving.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:20.120
Hello, everyone, welcome
to our Play2Connect event.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.120
Thank you for coming, we're
really excited to have you here.

00:02:24.603 --> 00:02:25.670
(crosstalk)

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.100
- [Woman] The light one.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.230
- Oh my gosh, look, you're
stopping the water flow.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:31.945
- All right, we're gonna
have parents and kids switch.

00:02:31.945 --> 00:02:34.530
- Now you need to start
capturing the animals.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.363
- And enter space

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:36.963
- Ah, put it in there again.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.780
I got it, I got it, I got it.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:40.613
- No, Dad.

00:02:40.613 --> 00:02:43.010
You build it on top of that.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.356
- All right, let's try to plant
seeds and see what happens.

00:02:45.356 --> 00:02:46.920
- (chuckling) What is happening?

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.985
- [Kid] I have a plan.

00:02:47.985 --> 00:02:48.818
- [Man] What are we gonna do?

00:02:48.818 --> 00:02:50.460
- I have to clear it myself.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.660
- We put some lights on.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:53.643
Some more torches?

00:02:54.629 --> 00:02:56.477
(crosstalk)

00:02:56.477 --> 00:02:57.990
- At home, I'm tutoring her,

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.570
now it's the other way around.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:02.240
- A few times I did big mistakes,

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.082
like flooded our cornfield.

00:03:05.082 --> 00:03:06.560
- It's not corn, wheat.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.670
- Oh, wheat, see?

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.140
- Did you enjoy the challenges?

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.073
- Especially the chicken farm we made.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.030
Why does it have a skeleton in it?

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.200
- It's a lot more fun than I thought.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.890
It's really interesting
watching him at work.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.860
- There's just more value here
than I think I had imagined,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.450
that it could be really good quality time.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.190
And I'm surprised at how
patient he was with me.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.470
- You liked me doing it,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.500
and then you were tellin' me, "good job."

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.560
That was cool.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.590
- It's really important
that we shift the trend

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.250
around video games and families,

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.280
and really start thinking
about video games

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.220
in terms of their potential

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.727
to contribute to our lives.

00:03:40.727 --> 00:03:42.202
(pig snorts)
(baby exclaims)

00:03:42.202 --> 00:03:43.700
Yeah, that's a pig!

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.814
Where's the pig?

00:03:44.814 --> 00:03:47.731
(grunts excitedly)

